2652	\begin{lemma}[Formalization support for reindexing a CL function]\label{lem:cl-reindex}
2653		\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.isCondLinearOn_reindex}
2654		\leanok
2655		\uses{def:cl-func, def:register-subspace}
2656		This is not a named statement of the source article; it isolates the transport of a CL function between register spaces used in the Lean proof of the conditional linearity of the Pauli question maps. Let $V' = \F^{n'}$ and $V = \F^{n}$, and let $f$ be an injective map of the coordinates of $V'$ into the coordinates of $V$, so that every register subspace of $V'$ is carried to a register subspace of $V$. Let $L$ be an $\ell$-level CL function on $V'$. Let $\tilde L \colon V \to V$ send $x$ to the vector whose coordinate at $f(k)$ is the $k$-th coordinate of $L\bigl( (x_{f(k)})_k \bigr)$ and whose coordinates outside the image of $f$ are zero. Then $\tilde L$ is an $\ell$-level CL function on $V$.
